[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2759927021","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104682#issuecomment-2759927021","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104682","id":2759927021,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6kgSTt","user":{"login":"MewPurPur","id":85438892,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1NDM4ODky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/85438892?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur","html_url":"https://github.com/MewPurPur","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-28T01:15:03Z","updated_at":"2025-03-28T01:15:03Z","body":"I'm not sure about the color scheme, we've created an expectation that anything with the blue/red color is a node. So seeing for example the blue KinematicCollision icon would confuse users about why it's not something you can add to your scene tree.\r\n\r\nThe icons themselves are great, but I think it might be better for now if the non-node ones use the standard white.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2759927021/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":2},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2759965368","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104682#issuecomment-2759965368","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104682","id":2759965368,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6kgbq4","user":{"login":"aaronfranke","id":1646875,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDY4NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1646875?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke","html_url":"https://github.com/aaronfranke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-28T01:55:33Z","updated_at":"2025-03-28T01:55:33Z","body":"@MewPurPur Good point. Follow-up question, then, is that useful? I think it makes more sense to color things based on dimension regardless of whether it's a node or not. Note that in most cases, you won't see nodes and non-nodes in the same place, for example the Create New Node dialog will only have nodes, and a resource picker will only have resources derived from the required type.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2759965368/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2760034248","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104682#issuecomment-2760034248","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104682","id":2760034248,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6kgsfI","user":{"login":"MewPurPur","id":85438892,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1NDM4ODky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/85438892?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur","html_url":"https://github.com/MewPurPur","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-28T02:39:59Z","updated_at":"2025-03-28T02:39:59Z","body":"I think dimensionality color-coding is useful, yeah. Right now, resources have a color scheme that doesn't respect dimensionality at all, and everything else uses white (aside from purple Tween, but that's a leftover from when it was a node). And some less relevant things have a chaotic color-coding, but this doesn't matter too much.\r\n\r\nI think it'd be good to set example, maybe have the colors be still bluish and reddish, but distinct enough to be clearly different from nodes? For example, a more saturated light blue and a more pinkish red? Then this can be used for other things, for example Shape2D and Shape3D's color coding I think could benefit from that.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2760034248/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2760991918","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104682#issuecomment-2760991918","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104682","id":2760991918,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6kkWSu","user":{"login":"groud","id":6093119,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwOTMxMTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6093119?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud","html_url":"https://github.com/groud","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-28T10:56:06Z","updated_at":"2025-03-28T10:56:06Z","body":"> I'm not sure about the color scheme, we've created an expectation that anything with the blue/red color is a node. So seeing for example the blue KinematicCollision icon would confuse users about why it's not something you can add to your scene tree.\r\n\r\nI have no strong opinion about that, but the resources don't appear in the \"add node\" dialog anyway. And nodes do not appear in the \"load resource\" dialog either. I think the confusion might only be there for the API. \r\n\r\n> I think it'd be good to set example, maybe have the colors be still bluish and reddish, but distinct enough to be clearly different from nodes? For example, a more saturated light blue and a more pinkish red? Then this can be used for other things, for example Shape2D and Shape3D's color coding I think could benefit from that.\r\n\r\nCould work, but it might be difficult to support light/dark theme and custom theme too. The more color we add, the more difficult it gets.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2760991918/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2761098682","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104682#issuecomment-2761098682","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104682","id":2761098682,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6kkwW6","user":{"login":"Lazy-Rabbit-2001","id":22123964,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMTIzOTY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22123964?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001","html_url":"https://github.com/Lazy-Rabbit-2001","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-28T11:28:14Z","updated_at":"2025-03-28T11:36:15Z","body":"Not sure if `World2D` and `World3D` in this pr better explains the meaning from the icon but, for me at least it doesn't if i were a new user because a new game developer with Godot would consider it as something big and small rather than an earth plus a moon. Maybe some transparent polygon or curves in the bigger circle as lands would make more sense? (Something like this:\r\n[![image.png](https://i.postimg.cc/fWcvQcxS/image.png)](https://postimg.cc/jCjfzJ3R)\r\n)\r\nMeanwhile, i don't think the `CollisionShape2D` can convey its meaning to users correctly, especially when they get confused on why the icon should be spatial instead of planar.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2761098682/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":3,"-1":1,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2761199909","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104682#issuecomment-2761199909","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104682","id":2761199909,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6klJEl","user":{"login":"MewPurPur","id":85438892,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1NDM4ODky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/85438892?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur","html_url":"https://github.com/MewPurPur","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-28T12:18:42Z","updated_at":"2025-03-28T12:18:42Z","body":"I didn't mean users would get confused between the two, but rather, they would see the blue/red non-nodes and be confused what they are and why they can't find them in the node dialog, or just think it's a node if they encounter it out of context.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2761199909/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2814009531","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104682#issuecomment-2814009531","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104682","id":2814009531,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6numC7","user":{"login":"MewPurPur","id":85438892,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1NDM4ODky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/85438892?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur","html_url":"https://github.com/MewPurPur","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-17T20:58:03Z","updated_at":"2025-04-17T20:58:13Z","body":"Messed around with some colors, I think `#8dddf9` and `#ffc8c8` could be good color codes for 2D and 3D of non-node objects in general. I'd suggest even eventually changing stuff like physics shapes to use that. When I first saw those, I was confused why they were all blue, even the 3D ones.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2814009531/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2819372446","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104682#issuecomment-2819372446","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104682","id":2819372446,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6oDDWe","user":{"login":"Mickeon","id":66727710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NzI3NzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66727710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Mickeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/events{/privacy}"